+|---|---|---|
+| `cargo test -p triplox` lib | 614 pass, 0 fail, 1 ignored | 615 pass, 0 fail, 1 ignored |
+| integration targets | 32 pass, 0 fail | 32 pass, 0 fail |
+| `cargo clippy -p triplox --all-targets` | clean | clean |
+
+(615 vs 614 is the new combined test. Both toggles are read from env at runtime, so clippy cannot
+differ between the arms; it was run once.)
+
+`cargo fmt` applied.
+
+## Benchmark
+
+`cargo bench --bench datalog_bench`, `VERTICES=2000 EDGE_PROB=0.01` (39764 edges, 45953 datoms per
+index), `RUNS=5`. Four arms — off / batched only / segments only / all on — interleaved in that
+order, three passes. `med` is the median of the three per-pass medians.
+
+Row counts are identical to the hand-off baseline in all four arms for all ten queries: triangles
+7821, out_degree 2000, in_degree_top 2000, neighbors_of_42 21, weight_filter 198, heavy_neighbors
+1908, the rest 1.
+
+Two other agents were benchmarking on the same machine throughout, so absolute times drift between
+passes (the `off` arm's triangles medians were 606 / 728 / 691 ms against a quiet-machine baseline
+of 537). Interleaving keeps the comparison fair; ratios are the number to read, not the absolute
+times, and anything under ~5 ms is noise.
+
